From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ejaaskel <esa.jaaskela@suomi24.fi>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 17:34:21 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] units: Mount /tmp with noexec

/tmp is world-writable and is a common staging area for dropped
payloads. Mounting it with noexec prevents executing binaries directly
from /tmp, complementing the nosuid and nodev options systemd already
sets.

Note that this may break software that extracts helper binaries or
compiles into /tmp, and scripts invoked as /tmp/script.sh. Such software
needs to use a different directory, or the option has to be dropped.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Sulka specific]
---
 units/tmp.mount | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/units/tmp.mount b/units/tmp.mount
index 9259981..92ed566 100644
--- a/units/tmp.mount
+++ b/units/tmp.mount
@@ -22,4 +22,4 @@ After=swap.target
 What=tmpfs
 Where=/tmp
 Type=tmpfs
-Options=mode=1777,strictatime,nosuid,nodev,size=50%%,nr_inodes=1m,x-systemd.graceful-option=usrquota
+Options=mode=1777,strictatime,nosuid,nodev,noexec,size=50%%,nr_inodes=1m,x-systemd.graceful-option=usrquota
